== English ==

===Pronunciation===
[[IPA]]: /'gʌnsəl/

===Noun===
'''gunsel'''
#A [[gun]]-[[carrying]] [[hoodlum]] or other [[criminal]].
#Young man kept for immoral purposes (Etymology: Yiddish [[gendzel]] or [[ganzel]]).

Note: The two meanings are believed to have originated concurrently but independently.

gunsel:
Or: gonsil / gonzel / gonsel : 
1. A 19 th century term of German and Yiddish (little goose) derivation for a young, inexperienced gay male. 

2. Street and prison slang for a passive-partner in anal-intercourse . See sodomite for synonyms.